From: Tim Douglas <me@timdoug.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ld testsuite: C33 Linux FDPIC expectations

A C33 Linux link is FDPIC, which, like FRV's and Blackfin's, refuses an
absolute address in a read-only segment: the loader relocates segments
independently, and text is shared.  Expect what those targets expect,
and the same of eh5, whose .cfi_personality and .cfi_lsda put absolute
addresses in .eh_frame; FRV and Blackfin skip it, their gas having no
CFI.  FDPIC makes .rofixup entries, never DT_TEXTREL.

Signed-off-by: Tim Douglas <me@timdoug.com>

diff --git a/ld/testsuite/ld-elf/comm-data5.d b/ld/testsuite/ld-elf/comm-data5.d
